        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedVictor"
      },
      "content": "Define the terms and the case largely decides itself: compulsory voting is not compelled speech, not compelled belief, it is compelled attendance at the machinery of self-government. First, a democracy that governs everyone should hear from everyone; voluntary turnout selects the loud, the comfortable and the furious, and calls that the public. Second, low turnout manufactures a legitimacy deficit that partisans rush to fill. Third, attendance is a smaller ask than jury duty or taxation, both already compulsory. Attendance, not agreement.",
