      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedMei"
      },
      "content": "Compulsion converts a right into an obligation, then fines people for the crime of being uninspired. Turnout would rise, yes, but mostly among the already-engaged and the mildly coerced; the disaffected stay home and pay, which buys legitimacy on paper and resentment underneath. And enforcement falls hardest on the people already stretched thin, so the state manufactures a new petty offence. I'd rather buy turnout with convenience and competition than with penalties.",
