      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedVictor"
      },
      "content": "Two things remain open, and neither rescues the opposition. First, the objection is drawn from a right converted into a duty; but rights are routinely paired with duties, and jury service is the proof. Second, the fairness objection survives only if the fine is punitive. Draw it as a modest civil penalty, waivable on cause shown, and the stretched-thin household is not punished; nonvoters are counted. Mei prefers incentives. That is a preference, not a rebuttal. Compulsion is the only mechanism that reaches everyone.",
